   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing, but it is a best guess: I did not verify the stereochemistry (amino acids assumed L, sugars assumed D-manno) or the sugar linkage positions against the image.\n\n**Macrocyclic peptide**, read N\u2192C: chloroacetyl-Phe-Val-Pro-Thr-Thr-Bip-NMeAla-Bip-NMeAla-Glu-Ala-Pro-Cys-Gly-Lys-NH2, where Bip is biphenylalanine. The chloroacetyl CH2 is bonded to the Cys sulfur by a thioether, which closes the ring.\n\n**Lys side chain**: the \u03b5-NH is acylated by a 4-substituted benzoyl group. Its para carbon carries CH=N\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013(CH2)3\u2013O\u2013, which is attached to the glycan.\n\n**Glycan**: all rings are read as mannopyranoses.\n- The reducing sugar is \u03b2-linked to the butanoyl O. Its O-3 carries an \u03b1-linked mannose that has a further \u03b11\u21922 mannose with a 6-O-phosphate.\n- The reducing sugar's O-6 carries an \u03b11\u21926 mannose, then another \u03b11\u21926 mannose.\n- That second \u03b11\u21926 mannose carries, at O-2, a terminal \u03b1-mannose whose C-6 is a CH2\u2013P(=O)(OH)2 phosphonate.\n\nSMILES: O=C(NNC(=O)CON=Cc1ccc(cc1)C(=O)NCCCC[C@H](NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@H](CS9)NC(=O)[C@@H]1CCCN1C(=O)[C@H](C)NC(=O)[C@H](CCC(=O)O)NC(=O)[C@H](C)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc2ccc(cc2)-c2ccccc2)NC(=O)[C@H](C)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc2ccc(cc2)-c2ccccc2)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)O)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)O)NC(=O)[C@@H]1CCCN1C(=O)[C@H](C(C)C)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2ccccc2)NC(=O)C9)C(N)=O)CCCO[C@H]1[C@@H](O)[C@@H](O[C@@H]5[C@@H](O[C@@H]6[C@@H](O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@@H](COP(=O)(O)O)O6)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@@H](CO)O5)[C@H](O)[C@@H](CO[C@@H]2[C@@H](O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@@H](CO[C@@H]3[C@@H](O[C@@H]4[C@@H](O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@@H](CP(=O)(O)O)O4)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@@H](CO)O3)O2)O1"
